<title>SPAIN: Banco Popular 1997 Q1 attr profit 16.14 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Banco Popular 1997 Q1 attr profit 16.14 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spain's Banco Popular for the first quarter of 1997:</p>
<p>				    (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	   16.14	vs     14.45</p>
<p> Net profit			    17.38	vs     15.48</p>
<p> Pretax profit			 26.32	vs     23.01</p>
<p> Ordinary margin		     60.10	vs     58.21</p>
<p> Operating margin		    31.61	vs     30.40</p>
<p> Net interest income		 44.05	vs     44.42</p>
<p>NOTE: Popular said in a statement that total assets were 3.49 trillion pesetas.</p>
<p>Customer loans were 2.26 trillion pesetas at the end of the first quarter and deposits were 2.64 trillion pesetas.</p>
<p>ROE rose to 20.43 percent form 19.48 in the year-earlier quarter and ROA rose to 2.01 percent from 1.86 percent.</p>
<p>Its tier-1 solvency coefficient is 13.51 percent.</p>
</text>
